"summary": "The file defines the k-colour triangle Ramsey number R_k(3) as the least n such that every k-colouring of the edges of K_n (on Fin n) has a monochromatic triangle. It states four results: R_k(3)^{1/k} → ∞; an explicit lower bound (c₀·k^{1/3}/log k)^k ≤ R_k(3) for k ≥ 2 together with the same limit; log R_k(3) lies between (1/3−ε)·k·log k and (1+ε)·k·log k eventually; and log R_k(3) = Θ(k log k). The main caveat is that the paper only asserts the existence of an absolute constant c, while the Lean statement fixes c₀ = 1/(6e^38), a value that is not in the excerpt. The upper-bound half of the log-sharp statements comes from the classical factorial bound, which the paper cites but does not prove in the excerpt.",
